# deml — Cursor rules (design system LOCKED)

You are working in the DEML control-plane repo. Visual design is owned by **deml-ui**.
The **new-from-the-start (NFTS) / heritage** look — **seven-color palette only** —
is **mandatory** for all future product UI. Do not drift back to Viking or
atelier-cream.

## Design system (required)

- **SoT:** `deml-ui` (sibling repo / `github:dataengineeringformachinelearning/deml-ui#main`).
- **Look:** NFTS / heritage — exact palette `#0066B2` `#3D3D3D` `#BDBDBD` `#121212`
  `#FFFFFF` `#3C7A4A` `#C41E3A`; 8px equal outer spacing; identical card/bento
  heights; fixed `--chart-aspect` (2.4); dual `data-theme`; WCAG 2.0 AA.
- **Docs:** `THEME.md` (locked SoT), `docs/DEML_UI.md`, `AGENTS.md` (Uniformity Law).
- **Storybook:** https://ui.deml.app

## Do

- Compose product pages with `app-banner`, `app-page-section`, `app-section-header`,
  `app-tile-board`, `app-dashboard-grid`, `app-card-grid`, `app-stat-card`,
  `app-chart-card`, `app-area-chart`, `app-bar-chart`.
- Keep Angular wrappers under `src/app/components` with `ViewEncapsulation.None`
  and **no** component CSS for design-system chrome (`styleUrl` / `styleUrls` /
  inline `styles` forbidden on DS wrappers and product pages).
- Use deml-ui CSS variables only (`--color-*`, `--palette-*`, `--space-*`,
  `--tile-*`, `--chart-*`, `--font-*`, `--tracking-*`).
- Keep **equal outer spacing** (8px multiples on all four sides) via `--tile-gap`
  / `--module-pad` / `.page-body` padding.
- Keep **identical card/bento/grid row heights** via `--tile-row-unit` + shared
  `--tile-gap` (siblings in a row stretch equally).
- Preserve chart aspect (`--chart-aspect: 2.4`); never squash or stretch plots;
  host series colors from the seven-color palette only, inside equal-height
  chart-cards.
- Preserve type hierarchy: display condensed tight (`--font-display` +
  `--tracking-display`); secondary/intro generous letter-spacing
  (`--tracking-eyebrow` / `--tracking-intro`); readable body (`--font-sans`).
- Prefer WCAG 2.0 AA: focus-visible, contrast, ≥44px hit targets, reduced motion.
- Dual theme via `data-theme="light"|"dark"` on `<html>` (`theme-color`:
  `#121212` / `#FFFFFF`).

## Do not

- Use or restore **Viking-UI** (`packages/viking-ui`,
  `@dataengineeringformachinelearning/viking-ui`, `viking-*`, `--viking-*`,
  void-black / electric `#2176ff` suite chrome).
- Restore **atelier-cream / limestone** hexes (`#2A2622`, `#E4DDD0`, `#F4F1EA`)
  or any hex outside the seven locked colors.
- Add Material, Bootstrap, Tailwind utility styling, or a parallel local design
  system / app-owned DS tokens.
- Hand-edit `backend/static/deml-ui.css` — sync from deml-ui via
  `scripts/sync_deml_ui_static.sh`.
- Put product UI back under `frontend/` (that folder is a Vercel rootDirectory
  shim only).
- Invent one-off / asymmetric spacing, free-resize charts, or `styleUrl` chrome
  on product pages.

## When changing visuals

1. Edit deml-ui `components/` + `styles/tokens.css` / `styles/base.css`.
2. `npm run build` in deml-ui (dist is consumed by github installs).
3. Bump deml’s `deml-ui` dependency / lockfile.
4. Sync Django static if templates need the new CSS.

**Locked:** NFTS / heritage seven-color deml-ui is mandatory — see `THEME.md`.
Agents must not regress to Viking or cream atelier looks.
